WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.336
- The kind of reforms and
incremental improvement

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.672
that the current system
is capable of delivering

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.140
are insufficient,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
so some form of radical
reorganization is required.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.014
And I would say that
to focus primarily

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.749
on where is power coalescing?

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:16.950
Is it observable?

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.685
Are there giant corporations

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.253
that are wealthier than nations?

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, that's an interesting
area to look at.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.625
Are there powerful
energy companies

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.962
that are still being
offered subsidies,

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.064
that are still being subsidized

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.732
when there is an energy crisis?

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.534
Is there a military
industrial complex

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.602
that's benefiting from war?

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:88% position:13%
Are there pharmaceutical
industries

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.905
that are benefiting
from medical crises?

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:42.075
These are all areas that
you might want to locate

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.543
as potential problems.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:47.947 align:start position:0%
So avert your eyes for a moment
from cultural differences

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:88% position:13%
and focus on where power
and financial cloud

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.619
and the ability to organize

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:88% position:13%
is currently centralized
and look at that.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:97% position:3%
That is the area that we
collectively need to address.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.995
(upbeat music)

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:97% position:3%
- All right, we're not
doing a normal intro today.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:12.372
I think you might know
this guy, Russell Brand.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:97% position:3%
Welcome to the Rubin Report
here in Locals in Miami

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.510
on your American tour.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.712
- Thanks for having me
on the Rubin Report.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.547
- Pretty good.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.381
We've got our own mugs.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.215
You can have that.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.049
You wanna keep that mug?

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.050
- Yes, please.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:24.984
I'd like you to sign it

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.719
and I'll keep it as a memento

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.388
of an already lovely occasion,

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.722
just arriving here
and meeting everyone.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.057
It's been so lovely.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.425
- You're bouncing all
over the place, man.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.927
It's been a wacky week.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.528
Do you have like a word

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.230
that would sum up
what has happened

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.498
since you got to America,

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.933
the Bill Maher thing,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then you've done 800
shows and all over the place.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.238 align:start size:81% position:19%
What word would
sum it up for you?

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.639
- Vicissitude.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.907
(Dave laughs)

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.977
Like it's sort of
like a vacillating,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:55.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
undulating, shape shifting,
state altering kind of.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.955
It's interesting,
isn't it, mate?

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:06.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because where rather
than the vanguard

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:10.497 align:start size:97% position:3%
of the political conversation
would you want to be?

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.465
Where else would you want to be?

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the truth is that I don't
do well with antagonism.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.138
I don't do well with it.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.806
I don't care for it much.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.078
I prize serenity very highly.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:81% position:19%
I don't really
particularly enjoy

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:33.720
being at the center
of incendiary matters

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.389
nor do I enjoy being criticized.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
Say, if you ask
someone for feedback,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.159
this is what I mean.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.160
"Oh, have you got any feedback?"

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:40.994
Do you know what
I actually mean?

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.462
Can you give me a series

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
of very sincere and
specific compliments now?

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:45.965
(Dave laughs)

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.133
That's what I mean,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:84% position:16%
sincere and specific
compliments.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
The way you did
that was brilliant,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.305
thank you.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.574
Then I can sort of
sit and reflect on it

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.943
as if like we're
studying something

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.646
that's objective and external.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.749
I don't like to feel
attacked in particular,

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.684
perhaps nobody does.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:09.455
Long ago, due to the
nature of a celebrity,

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.691
I have broadly elected

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.128
to extract myself from
the discourse about me,

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
deciding as is
suggested in my program,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.435
what other people think of
me is none of my business.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.304
What other people think of
me is none of my business.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.307
You can do what you want
in your mind, that's yours.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.775
Or you could even
say what you want,

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.543
it's none of my business,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.178
it's abstract.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:36.115
But of course, like on the
level of how I actually feel,

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:97% position:3%
I am, like all of us I'm sure,
a well-intentioned person

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.856
and I am optimistic
about human beings

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:48.094 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I'm trying to do something
that I feel is important.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.496
And perhaps I hope
I'm doing it well,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.465
but of course with
no way of knowing.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.967
- Isn't it kind of funny?

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:57.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like someone that doesn't
court the controversy

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then you have a moment
like that, Real Time moment...

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.608
Which actually, why don't we
just throw to it real quick.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:02.809
Everyone's seen it
a million times,

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.643
we'll throw to it.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.477
(audience laughs)

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.945
- It's disingenuous

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
to claim that the biases that
are exhibited on Fox News

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:10.950
are any different from the
biases exhibited on MSNBC.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.884
(audience applauds)

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.819
It's difficult to suggest

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.287
that these corporations operate

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.322
as anything other
than mouthpieces

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.692
for their affiliate owners
in BlackRock and Vanguard.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.362
And unless we start to embrace,

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.797
and also mate, like
just spiritually,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.333
if I may use that word
in your great country,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.869
we have to take responsibility

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.537
for our own perspective.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.473
I've been on the MSNBC, mate.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:36.042
It was propaganda, it's
nut crackery in there.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
I went on a show
called "Morning Joe."

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.912 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was absurd the
way they carried on.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:40.713
- Good morning Joe.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:41.948
That's not it.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:42.782
- I dunno what it was.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.017
It wasn't morning,

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:44.951
there was no one
called Joe there,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.452
no one could concentrate,

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.021
they didn't understand the
basic tenets of journalism.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:51.791 align:start size:97% position:3%
No one was willing to stick
up for genuine American heroes

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.326
like Edward Snowden.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.828
And no one was willing to
talk about Julian Assange

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.531
and what he suffered trying
to bring real journalism

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.266
to the American people.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.701
(audience applauds)

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think to sit within
the castle of MSNBC

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.141
throwing rocks at Fox
News is ludicrous.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.909
Make MSNBC better.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
- The moment that you give
me a specific example,

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.080
an actual example.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.014
- Okay, I'll give you one-

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.249
- Just wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.651
- We need just a
specific example-

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.585
- How about.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.087
- Calm down, (indistinct)

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.222
I'd like to hear a
specific example,

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.390
a proof of a specific example

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.626 align:start size:88% position:13%
of an MSNBC
correspondent or anchor

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:29.796
being on television saying
something they knew was false

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and were saying behind the
scenes to his people...

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.366
I'm allowed to go out,

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.235
and we know that the
election wasn't stolen

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.170
or something equivalent-

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.571
- Giving a specific example-

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
- But I will go on television
and say the opposite.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:42.875
I will lie.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.077
- [Russell] When's my answer?

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:46.245
- Well, just gimme
the specific example.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.180 align:start size:88% position:13%
- [Russell] I understand
the basic point-

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.114
- Gimme a specific example.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.549
- All right.
- I'm with you.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.484
I think it's a false
equivalency, Russell.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:52.919
- That's your own
biases, plainly.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.120
- It's not about bias.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.655
It's a false equivalency

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.557 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause you don't
actually know anything

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start position:0%
about any of these organizations
you're talking about.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.527
You've been on MSNBC
once, big fuckin' deal.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.929
(audience laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
- My darling, it was
more than enough.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:07.100
- You don't have a
single actual fact.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.568
- Do you want an example?

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.402
Do you want an example?

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.570
- Yes.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
- The ludicrous
outrageous criticisms

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:15.174
of Joe Rogan around Ivermectin,

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.710 align:start position:0%
which we're deliberately
referring to as a horse medicine

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
when they know it's
an effective medicine-

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:20.747
- Non-responsive.

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:22.081
- [Bill Maher] That's
not a bad example.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Rachel Maddow
turning up on the TV

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:26.085 align:start position:0%
saying if you take this vaccine,
you're not gonna get it,

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
when it hadn't been clinically
trialed for transmission-

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.021
- Nonresponsive.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.223
- You have to listen.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.425
Do you think you
can improve America

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:36.195 align:start size:97% position:3%
by determinedly and
avowedly condemning Fox News

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.597
without acknowledging

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're participating
in the same game?

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.634 align:start size:88% position:13%
Did you not just listen
to Bernie Sanders?

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
Someone who plainly,
legitimately believes
in this country

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.572
and believes it's
possible to change

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:48.474
but is bound by corruption,

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.176
is bound by the lobbying system.

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.244
(audience applauds)

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:53.079
It surely is clear to you, Bill,

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:57.049
as one of the great pundits
and experts and comic voices

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.185 align:start size:84% position:16%
that systemic
change is required.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:01.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
Money has to be taken
out of politics.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.156
We need new political systems

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:06.259 align:start size:88% position:13%
that genuinely represent
ordinary Americans

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:09.095
so that we can overcome
cultural differences.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.797
(audience applauds)

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:13.533
And bickering about
which propagandist
network is the worst

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:16.235
is not gonna save a
single American life

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.638
nor improve the life of
a single American child,

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.840 align:start size:97% position:3%
not gonna improve America's
standing in the world.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.909
And the world needs
a strong America.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.143
I'll tell you that.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:24.977
(audience applauds)

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:25.912
I'll tell you that.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:27.046
So you have an obligation,

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:29.782 align:start size:84% position:16%
a duty not to
condemn these people.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.250
- You weren't being a dick.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.485
I mean, that's the thing.

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.587
You were trying to say
something very true,

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:37.623 align:start size:81% position:19%
something that
most of us we know

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.592
about media and everything,

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:40.693
but then it gets turned

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.463 align:start size:88% position:13%
into like this
destruction of this guy.

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:45.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I probably even
feed into some of that

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:46.933
when I covered it on my show.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.935
Like, man, that guy kind
of deserved to get wrecked.

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:50.369
But it wasn't really about him.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.771
You weren't trying
to make it about him,

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:53.239
that was very clear.

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:57.643 align:start position:0%
- I was astonished that anybody
is willing to go to the mat

00:07:58.511 --> 00:07:59.879
for that set of values anymore.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.948 align:start size:84% position:16%
But of course, I
know that people are.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.115
And yeah, I don't like the idea

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.318 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I'm being
impolite to a person.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:08.488 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's not in accordance
with my values.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:09.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But you weren't
really being impolite.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.557 align:start size:81% position:19%
You were being
passionate, right?

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.459
Like you weren't rude
to him, I don't think.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you were confident
in what you were saying

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:17.964
and it needed to be said.

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:21.834
- Yeah, I feel we can't move
forward with the conversation.

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:24.303
Like it happens in
politics, doesn't it?

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.572
When they say, "oh, well
this is only happening,

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.341 align:start size:88% position:13%
the last administration
done that"

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:31.577
or "this is because CNN
or Fox News or whoever."

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.746
It's like, well,
why don't we focus

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:36.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
on what we are
contributing individually

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.384
or if we claim to be
the representative

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:42.388 align:start position:0%
of some sort of movement, class,
culture, or advocacy group,

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:43.890
perhaps then we can look...

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
If we claim to speak
on behalf of them

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:48.327 align:start size:84% position:16%
and certainly I
make no such claim,

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:52.798 align:start size:97% position:3%
then we should look after
ourselves and our own conduct.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.234
And because as Gandhi said,

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.737 align:start size:84% position:16%
"I find I am such a
sinner in my own life,

00:08:57.737 --> 00:09:00.506
I'm not confident when it
comes to judging others."

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:02.375
I try to monitor my own behavior

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.677
but I am engaged in punditry,

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:06.412
I am engaged in commentary.

00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:10.449
And as I said I suppose
in that conversation,

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:12.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's not like I particularly
align with Fox News

00:09:12.919 --> 00:09:14.086
as an institution.

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:15.388 align:start size:88% position:13%
In fact, I have a
rather colorful history

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:16.822
with that organization.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:17.990
- Right, right, right, right.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.026 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when you were
preparing for the show

00:09:20.026 --> 00:09:21.260
were they telling you...

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.862
Obviously, they do a
pre-interview with you

00:09:22.862 --> 00:09:24.830
or you passed that point?

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.200
- We kept trying to do it
but I kept not doing it.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.169
I kept not doing
the pre-interview.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:33.339
- Right, but you knew what the
topics were gonna be, right?

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.674
- No, I knew like...

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:35.875
What happened,

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:39.011 align:start size:88% position:13%
they said that that
might come up actually.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:42.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
I thought that they said we
would talk about the pandemic.

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:45.217
And then I think that they said
that there was a possibility

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.587 align:start size:88% position:13%
that the changing nature
of the relationship

00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:50.389
between Fox News and
Trump would come up.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:55.394 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so I suppose it was within
the orbit of that topic,

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:59.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
the contretemp around
the distinctions

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:02.535
between neoliberal
establishment media

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:06.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
and neo-conservative
establishment media
was discussed.

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:07.773
- Yeah, it was so interesting

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:09.342
because when he was
trying to get you

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:10.743
like, give me the one, right?

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.211
Like he was trying to,

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:13.646
"give me one time that
they intentionally lied."

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:15.982
And it's like, man, we
could do this all day.

00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.750
Very fine people on both sides.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.518
Brett Kavanaugh's
a serial rapist.

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.087
The Covington kids are racist.

00:10:21.087 --> 00:10:22.822
I mean, I do this on
my show every day.

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:24.523
You went with the Rogan one

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:28.027
and it's like he just
didn't have much after.

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:28.961
- He wanted to, I suppose-

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:30.129
- Does it get to that point

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.064 align:start size:88% position:13%
of like it's weird
that anyone defends it?

00:10:32.064 --> 00:10:34.000
Is that really what you
think this is about?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.868
I'm starting to
come to that too,

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:38.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
that it's hard to
defend at this point.

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:40.840
- This is where I'm at, Dave.

00:10:42.041 --> 00:10:46.879
I'm at why don't
we now acknowledge

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:50.950 align:start size:88% position:13%
that there are different
ways of being a human

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:54.020
and call a kind of truce

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:56.222 align:start size:84% position:16%
and accept that
there are some people

00:10:56.222 --> 00:10:58.557
for the sake of simplicity;

00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:01.794
that there are progressive
ways of being a human being,

00:11:01.794 --> 00:11:04.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are traditional ways
of being a human being,

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:07.166
neither of those ways are wrong.

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:09.568
Why don't we allow one another

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:12.138 align:start size:84% position:16%
to express ourselves
how we want to

00:11:12.138 --> 00:11:15.408
within the obvious
bounds of consent?

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:19.211 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then perhaps we can
organize different alliances

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:20.780
so that we can organize

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.249
around the systems
of centralized power

00:11:23.249 --> 00:11:28.254
that will else-wise continue
to dominate and annihilate.

00:11:29.622 --> 00:11:30.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Do you sense that that's
happening right now?

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:32.391
I mean, me living
here in Florida.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.527
I mean, look, I'm gay, I'm
married, I have two kids.

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:36.328
Like this is the freedom place.

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:37.863
They make it seem like

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:39.899
it's the place of right wing
crazy people and everything.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:43.202
I'm freaking loved here and I
love it right back, it's wild.

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:45.571 align:start size:81% position:19%
- But no one cares
about being gay

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:47.406
or being married
or having two kids?

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.241
- No, it was freaking Halloween.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:50.576
We took our kids in strollers,

00:11:50.576 --> 00:11:53.612 align:start size:88% position:13%
met every neighbor
within 10 square blocks.

00:11:53.612 --> 00:11:55.548
Not one weird comment site.

00:11:55.548 --> 00:11:56.982
Nobody cares.

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:58.718
That's happening right here,

00:11:58.718 --> 00:12:01.387
I think what you're calling for.

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:03.289 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it's not
happening everywhere.

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:08.828
- Do you feel that that
would be able to escalate

00:12:08.828 --> 00:12:10.796
through the various expressions

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:15.468
of like every letter
of the LGBTQ+ moniker?

00:12:15.468 --> 00:12:17.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I mean, I personally
have nothing to do

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:19.505
with that whole thing.

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:22.842 align:start position:0%
I happen to be gay and I'm
married to a guy and that's it.

00:12:22.842 --> 00:12:24.310
I only represent myself

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:27.012 align:start size:97% position:3%
as I think you probably only
represent Russell Brand.

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:28.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when they try to
put all these letters-

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.982
- If even-
- Right.

00:12:29.982 --> 00:12:31.250
(Dave laughs)

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.752
- Bits of Russell
Brand I represent

00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:35.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there are parts of that
guy I want nothing to do with.

00:12:35.087 --> 00:12:36.489 align:start position:0%
- Who's the true representation
of Russell Brand?

00:12:36.489 --> 00:12:38.758
- There are so many of us.

00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:40.126
"Goodbye Ruby Tuesday,"

00:12:40.126 --> 00:12:41.327
who could put a name on you

00:12:41.327 --> 00:12:42.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you change
with every new day?

00:12:42.895 --> 00:12:44.730
- There you go.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.133
Yeah, I don't know that...

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:48.634
Well, let's put it this way,

00:12:48.634 --> 00:12:53.272
if there was a trans person
walking around the town,

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:55.074
I don't think they would
be ridiculed or anything.

00:12:55.074 --> 00:12:57.777
I think people basically are
just kind of live and let live.

00:12:57.777 --> 00:13:00.613
Politics is making us all
kind of nuts at this point.

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:02.014
- Politics and the culture.

00:13:02.014 --> 00:13:05.251 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I cannot see it
anymore as inadvertent.

00:13:05.251 --> 00:13:08.587
It feels to me that it
must be a requirement

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:11.223
of sustaining the
systems of power

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:14.426 align:start size:88% position:13%
that benefit, for
example, in the pandemic

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:17.463
in the obvious observable and
trackable ways financially

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:18.831 align:start size:81% position:19%
and through the
ability to surveil

00:13:18.831 --> 00:13:21.233
and introduce new regulation,

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:26.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
they must benefit
from ongoing conflict.

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:28.073
- So it's a needed
piece of the puzzle-

00:13:28.073 --> 00:13:30.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It feels to me
like it is, actually.

00:13:30.843 --> 00:13:33.479
And so my sense is that

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:38.617
like there cannot be one
homogenized version of...

00:13:38.617 --> 00:13:40.820
There cannot be a uni-culture,

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.155
there cannot be
a unipolar world,

00:13:43.155 --> 00:13:46.292
you cannot have a new hegemonic.

00:13:46.292 --> 00:13:48.627
There must be the acceptance

00:13:48.627 --> 00:13:53.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
of I would say sort of
compatible, interconnected,

00:13:56.335 --> 00:13:59.605
localized systems of governance

00:13:59.605 --> 00:14:02.641
that as much freedom,
as much democracy,

00:14:02.641 --> 00:14:06.145 align:start size:84% position:16%
as much community
and the systems of...

00:14:06.145 --> 00:14:08.848
My sense is, and again
it's just a vague one;

00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:10.182
the systems of aggregation

00:14:10.182 --> 00:14:11.684
benefit people at
the top of them,

00:14:11.684 --> 00:14:13.886 align:start size:88% position:13%
from agriculture through
industrialization

00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:15.154
through technology.

00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:17.089
Whilst there are obvious
benefits to agriculture

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:18.257
to a population at large,

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:19.625
the most significant gains

00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:21.527
are experienced at the
top of those systems.

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:24.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the amendments that
are possible are not made,

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.798
like industrialization.

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:26.999
And even the sort of like

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:29.735
the so-called white
goods revolution

00:14:29.735 --> 00:14:30.903
in this country in the 1950s,

00:14:30.903 --> 00:14:32.838 align:start size:84% position:16%
"you are gonna
have plenty of time

00:14:32.838 --> 00:14:34.139
with your new dishwasher."

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:36.308
And it's like, do we
have any more time?

00:14:36.308 --> 00:14:40.346
Are there different ways of
deploying these sets of tools

00:14:40.346 --> 00:14:43.616
or is everything subtly and
unconsciously being used

00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:46.585
in the service of
a particular idea

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:49.288
that's oddly centralizing?

00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:50.856
- Yeah, Peter Thiel always says,

00:14:50.856 --> 00:14:54.326
"they promised us flying cars
and we got 140 characters."

00:14:54.326 --> 00:14:57.229
In essence, we've sort
of stopped innovating now

00:14:57.229 --> 00:14:59.398 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we're just
doom-scrolling all day long.

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:02.134
Remember back in our day
when the internet stopped?

00:15:02.134 --> 00:15:04.236
You'd go to a page and it
would stop at the bottom.

00:15:04.236 --> 00:15:05.504 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Oh, yeah.
- Remember that?

00:15:05.504 --> 00:15:06.939
And then they got rid of that

00:15:06.939 --> 00:15:10.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you just scroll forever
and it never stops.

00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:12.111
And you're looking for
more, more craziness.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:13.946
- Yes, it's nihilistic.

00:15:13.946 --> 00:15:17.116
- I kind of sense that
you're more libertarian

00:15:17.116 --> 00:15:18.384
than anything else.

00:15:18.384 --> 00:15:19.818
Even though people
are always like...

00:15:19.818 --> 00:15:20.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
The people on the
right are always like,

00:15:20.786 --> 00:15:22.488
"he's a lefty but I like him,"

00:15:22.488 --> 00:15:23.923
something like that, right?

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:24.857
That's what they
do with Bill Maher.

00:15:24.857 --> 00:15:26.959
- I'm a lefty you kinda like.

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:27.960
(Dave laughs)

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.361
- There could be
a movie in that.

00:15:29.361 --> 00:15:30.930
I think they said that in that.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.665
But I sense you're mostly like,

00:15:32.665 --> 00:15:34.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're talking about
decentralization,

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:35.401
you're talking about
local communities,

00:15:35.401 --> 00:15:37.436 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're talking about
taking power away

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:38.604
and that kind of stuff.

00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:40.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like you're mostly
just live and let live.

00:15:40.139 --> 00:15:42.308
I mean the show is
stay free, right?

00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:45.077
- Yes, I suppose when people
talk about libertarianism,

00:15:45.077 --> 00:15:47.546
sometimes there's the sort
of is there the suggestion

00:15:47.546 --> 00:15:50.749
that we do not have
a duty and obligation

00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:52.985
to love and care
for one another?

00:15:52.985 --> 00:15:55.754
I suppose I don't feel that
that needs to be mandated

00:15:55.754 --> 00:15:57.556
at the end of a gun,

00:15:57.556 --> 00:16:01.193 align:start size:88% position:13%
that people can love one
another consensually.

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:05.030
And that we can organize in
various different publics,

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.267
we can have the maximum
amount of democracy,

00:16:08.267 --> 00:16:11.170 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we can honor the highest
aspects of our nature.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.838
That broadly speaking,

00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:15.841 align:start position:0%
I would respond sympathetically
to a person suffering

00:16:15.841 --> 00:16:17.076
if I could see them.

00:16:17.076 --> 00:16:18.310
What I'm beginning to feel

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:22.681 align:start size:81% position:19%
is that we have
become disjointed.

00:16:22.681 --> 00:16:25.150
There's been an aberration

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the conditions
of our origin.

00:16:27.286 --> 00:16:28.687
There's nothing in our evolution

00:16:28.687 --> 00:16:30.589
that suggests that we
would be able to live

00:16:30.589 --> 00:16:32.791 align:start size:84% position:16%
in societies of
300 million people,

00:16:32.791 --> 00:16:34.693
let alone 7 billion people.

00:16:34.693 --> 00:16:36.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
Whilst that is
part of the reality

00:16:36.528 --> 00:16:38.564
that we are on a rock
in infinite space,

00:16:38.564 --> 00:16:40.065
we are also in communities.

00:16:40.065 --> 00:16:41.533
And I like that phrase

00:16:41.533 --> 00:16:43.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I think I heard from
Helena Norberg-Hodge,

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:46.105
"act local, think global."

00:16:46.105 --> 00:16:47.339
(Russell chuckles)

00:16:47.339 --> 00:16:49.208
So like we can have
as much democracy

00:16:49.208 --> 00:16:50.709
in our community as possible,

00:16:50.709 --> 00:16:52.077
that we allow people

00:16:52.077 --> 00:16:54.446 align:start size:97% position:3%
to organize their communities
however they want to

00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:57.383
unless it has a negative
impact on another community

00:16:57.383 --> 00:16:58.751
or the individuals
within that community

00:16:58.751 --> 00:17:00.119
are not happy with it.

00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:01.787
And that we have to accept

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:04.156 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there are many different
ways of being human,

00:17:04.156 --> 00:17:06.725
traditional ways, new
and emergent ways,

00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:09.928 align:start position:0%
new roles, new identities allow
people to be who they are,

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:12.197
allow people to have as much
democracy in their schools

00:17:12.197 --> 00:17:14.199 align:start size:84% position:16%
as much as the
democracy in their...

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:17.436 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even law and order
ought to be democratic.

00:17:17.436 --> 00:17:18.904
In my country, for
example, I heard...

00:17:18.904 --> 00:17:21.073 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like I respect very much
people that work in services

00:17:21.073 --> 00:17:23.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause I understand
the value of sacrifice

00:17:23.375 --> 00:17:25.344
and I have friends that are
working the police force,

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:26.812
thank God.

00:17:26.812 --> 00:17:30.849 align:start size:97% position:3%
And like I feel that wouldn't
it be good if the forces,

00:17:30.849 --> 00:17:34.920
even law enforcements, a
phrase that's got some...

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.923
As a true anarchist libertarian,

00:17:37.923 --> 00:17:39.291
that I have some issues with,

00:17:39.291 --> 00:17:41.827
because who do you mandate to?

00:17:41.827 --> 00:17:43.095
Because the relationship

00:17:43.095 --> 00:17:45.297
between sovereignty
and the governed

00:17:45.297 --> 00:17:47.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
is traditionally being
you give us taxes,

00:17:47.132 --> 00:17:50.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
we won't let you get killed
by bandits or whatever.

00:17:50.903 --> 00:17:51.837
But me, personally-

00:17:51.837 --> 00:17:52.738
- That would be the basis of it.

00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:54.206
(both laugh)

00:17:54.206 --> 00:17:56.175
- Yeah, you know those bandits,
they could get you any time.

00:17:56.175 --> 00:17:58.644 align:start size:97% position:3%
Give us some of your money
and we'll protect you from it.

00:17:58.644 --> 00:18:00.179
But what I feel, Dave,

00:18:00.179 --> 00:18:01.980
is that it would be nice

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:05.651 align:start position:0%
if there were consensual
policing, consensual governance.

00:18:05.651 --> 00:18:08.353
You live in the area like
it's sort of localism,

00:18:08.353 --> 00:18:09.154
like this phrase.

00:18:09.154 --> 00:18:10.522
They are supposed to...

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:12.057 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you have like particular
phrases and ideas

00:18:12.057 --> 00:18:14.660
that have sort of stayed in
the sphere of your awareness

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.161
for a long while

00:18:16.161 --> 00:18:17.362
and they start to become part
of your personal philosophy?

00:18:17.362 --> 00:18:18.864
In my case,

00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:21.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
when Gandhi said the point
of Indian independence,

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:23.202
"this is a country
of 70,000 villages,

00:18:23.202 --> 00:18:25.504
each one should be
fully independent

00:18:25.504 --> 00:18:27.106
trading only where necessary,

00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:28.540 align:start size:84% position:16%
running and
governing themselves.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.576
There's no point in us
kicking out the British

00:18:30.576 --> 00:18:34.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
then replicating the
very institutions
that they installed."

00:18:34.613 --> 00:18:37.850
And it seems that we are
doing this now globally.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.419
Sets of institutionalized power,

00:18:40.419 --> 00:18:41.854 align:start size:81% position:19%
whether they're
corporate or state

00:18:41.854 --> 00:18:44.022 align:start position:0%
that don't allow ordinary people
to have very much freedom.

00:18:44.022 --> 00:18:45.224
- It's interesting

00:18:45.224 --> 00:18:46.692 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause you're basically
I think selling me,

00:18:46.692 --> 00:18:48.861
from an American perspective,
you're selling Federalism.

