foreigners have been sold off

00:26:39.631 --> 00:26:40.832
when they privatized everything.

00:26:40.832 --> 00:26:43.101 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm not suggesting
renationalize,

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:44.936
community own their assets,

00:26:44.936 --> 00:26:46.371
community decide

00:26:46.371 --> 00:26:48.306 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether or not they want
sewage dumped in their rivers.

00:26:48.306 --> 00:26:50.375
Maximum amount of democracy,

00:26:50.375 --> 00:26:52.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
maximum amount of respect
for the environment,

00:26:52.611 --> 00:26:54.012
maximum amount of respect,

00:26:54.012 --> 00:26:55.580
that's what we aspire to.

00:26:55.580 --> 00:26:57.248 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it seems though,
across the aisle.

00:26:57.248 --> 00:26:58.249 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You're a
federalist, I love it.

00:26:58.249 --> 00:26:59.451
I love it,

00:26:59.451 --> 00:27:00.385
you're a federalist-
- Ah, that's what I am.

00:27:00.385 --> 00:27:01.319
Maximum amount of democracy-

00:27:01.319 --> 00:27:02.487
- I know you don't want labels

00:27:02.487 --> 00:27:03.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I mean you believe
in local control

00:27:03.955 --> 00:27:05.724 align:start size:88% position:13%
and people making
decisions for themselves

00:27:05.724 --> 00:27:07.926
with some limited structure.

00:27:07.926 --> 00:27:09.094
- Yeah.

00:27:09.094 --> 00:27:10.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
And always being
aware of the tendency

00:27:10.662 --> 00:27:12.263
to rampant corporatism

00:27:12.263 --> 00:27:14.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
because at the moment
that is what's happening.

00:27:14.299 --> 00:27:16.034
And when people are
claiming localism,

00:27:16.034 --> 00:27:17.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're sort of
turning a blind eye

00:27:17.769 --> 00:27:21.473
to the way that corporatism
can exploit that localism

00:27:21.473 --> 00:27:23.341
if not properly undertaken.

00:27:23.341 --> 00:27:24.843
If there's any alliance at all,

00:27:24.843 --> 00:27:29.047
it's in order to confront
gargantuan corporate power.

00:27:29.047 --> 00:27:30.281
- So as you've been on this-

00:27:30.281 --> 00:27:31.783
- And get money out of
politics altogether,

00:27:31.783 --> 00:27:33.184 align:start size:81% position:19%
should we offer
that into the mix?

00:27:33.184 --> 00:27:34.686
- Yeah.

00:27:34.686 --> 00:27:36.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
Isn't it funny that that was
a big thing 20 years ago-

00:27:36.655 --> 00:27:37.889
- Where did that go?

00:27:37.889 --> 00:27:38.790
- And now it's just gone.

00:27:38.790 --> 00:27:40.191
Remember that?

00:27:40.191 --> 00:27:41.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
- The politicians
decided, hold on a minute,

00:27:41.426 --> 00:27:42.727 align:start size:81% position:19%
let's leave the
money in politics.

00:27:42.727 --> 00:27:44.629
- Somebody's gotta
pay for these states.

00:27:44.629 --> 00:27:46.498
You ever go out to dinner in DC?

00:27:46.498 --> 00:27:47.599
These people are eating well.

00:27:47.599 --> 00:27:48.433
- Are they?

00:27:48.433 --> 00:27:49.267
- Yeah.

00:27:49.267 --> 00:27:50.769
- Of course, they are.

00:27:50.769 --> 00:27:52.003
Have you ever been to any of
like the big globalist things?

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:53.438 align:start size:75% position:25%
You ever get...
- No.

00:27:53.438 --> 00:27:54.372 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You've never been
invited to any of those?

00:27:54.372 --> 00:27:55.540
Sometimes they bring in celebs.

00:27:55.540 --> 00:27:57.042
- They might have picked up the-

00:27:57.042 --> 00:27:59.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
- But maybe before you
were like fully, you know-

00:27:59.077 --> 00:28:01.913
- Yeah, no, never, actually.

00:28:01.913 --> 00:28:04.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe but I can't remember
ever going anywhere

00:28:04.883 --> 00:28:08.486
and thinking this
is reprehensible.

00:28:08.486 --> 00:28:11.289
- What was the moment that
you got sort of into this,

00:28:11.289 --> 00:28:12.924
the politics side of this thing?

00:28:12.924 --> 00:28:15.093 align:start size:88% position:13%
I know you're not really
political in a way

00:28:15.093 --> 00:28:18.163 align:start size:88% position:13%
but you clearly are
talking about politics.

00:28:18.163 --> 00:28:21.466
I mean, you're an
actor and a comic.

00:28:21.466 --> 00:28:22.901
Like was that kind
of always in you

00:28:22.901 --> 00:28:24.636 align:start size:88% position:13%
or was there like a
moment that it happened?

00:28:24.636 --> 00:28:26.705
Did COVID kind of escalate it?

00:28:26.705 --> 00:28:27.939
- No.

00:28:27.939 --> 00:28:29.441
Actor, comic, that's a
type of a job, isn't it?

00:28:29.441 --> 00:28:32.644
Like a comedian, actually for
me is sort of beyond a job,

00:28:32.644 --> 00:28:33.812
that's a religion.

00:28:33.812 --> 00:28:34.746
- Yeah.

00:28:34.746 --> 00:28:35.647
- That's sort of a purpose.

00:28:35.647 --> 00:28:36.581
It's a perspective.

00:28:36.581 --> 00:28:38.683
Actor is a type of a job for me.

00:28:38.683 --> 00:28:43.688
For me, my worldview is
part of my condition,

00:28:48.626 --> 00:28:50.495
it's part of where I come from,

00:28:50.495 --> 00:28:53.565
it's part of what I believe in.

00:28:53.565 --> 00:28:55.900
And becoming an actor,

00:28:55.900 --> 00:28:57.936
that's just simply opportunism.

00:28:57.936 --> 00:28:59.771
I was doing standup comedy,

00:28:59.771 --> 00:29:02.907
I got jobs on the TV
as a result of that,

00:29:02.907 --> 00:29:04.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
I then got off the movies,
all of these things.

00:29:04.843 --> 00:29:08.113 align:start size:97% position:3%
Oh, these are all
interesting, exciting things.

00:29:08.113 --> 00:29:11.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by God, were they
exciting and for a while.

00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:14.953
But what would we be?

00:29:16.855 --> 00:29:18.089
Look, I sometimes think this,

00:29:18.089 --> 00:29:19.624
if it didn't exist,
would I invent it?

00:29:19.624 --> 00:29:22.227
Like if there was no such
thing as a movie industry,

00:29:22.227 --> 00:29:23.661
would I go, "why don't we spend

00:29:23.661 --> 00:29:25.864 align:start size:97% position:3%
like a hundred million
dollars telling this story?"

00:29:25.864 --> 00:29:27.398
And what we'll do

00:29:27.398 --> 00:29:28.666
is we'll get to trailers at
four o'clock in the morning.

00:29:28.666 --> 00:29:29.834
I'll stay in there
most of the time,

00:29:29.834 --> 00:29:31.035
then I'll pop out for a bit

00:29:31.035 --> 00:29:33.004
and I'll like do a
little bit of acting.

00:29:33.004 --> 00:29:34.472
No, what I want to do

00:29:34.472 --> 00:29:37.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
is communicate truthfully
and connect people.

00:29:37.542 --> 00:29:39.010
If anything,

00:29:39.010 --> 00:29:43.081
it's like a kind of secular
and inclusive evangelism

00:29:43.081 --> 00:29:47.085 align:start position:0%
that's deeply devout and
accepting of the different ways

00:29:47.085 --> 00:29:48.586
that people might find God.

00:29:48.586 --> 00:29:50.522 align:start size:97% position:3%
That each of us are gonna
have our own journey to God.

00:29:50.522 --> 00:29:52.023
That doesn't mean

00:29:52.023 --> 00:29:53.992 align:start size:97% position:3%
that people might not be
part of a religious community

00:29:53.992 --> 00:29:55.760
or indeed a global faith,

00:29:55.760 --> 00:29:59.697
but that if we do not have
a connection to something

00:29:59.697 --> 00:30:01.833
that I would call
sublime or divine,

00:30:01.833 --> 00:30:04.269 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we are likely to
become lost in materialism,

00:30:04.269 --> 00:30:06.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
individualism, nihilism,
and progressivism.

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:09.507
And by progressivism I don't
mean cultural progressivism,

00:30:09.507 --> 00:30:12.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
the idea that human
beings are on this journey

00:30:12.243 --> 00:30:13.845
to better and better stuff.

00:30:13.845 --> 00:30:15.513 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that doesn't
seem to be happening

00:30:15.513 --> 00:30:17.015
other than I would say

00:30:17.015 --> 00:30:19.083
through the false markers
of medicine and technology.

00:30:19.083 --> 00:30:21.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
And although they are
marvelous, great miracles.

00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:24.489
- Is that what you're up
to more than anything else?

00:30:24.489 --> 00:30:27.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
That we're just like in this
lack of truth right now?

00:30:27.225 --> 00:30:29.828
And even to bring it back
to the Real Time moment,

00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:32.130
like you were trying
to say something true

00:30:32.130 --> 00:30:34.732
in a culture war where
nothing is true, right?

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:36.267
Like you do your show every day,

00:30:36.267 --> 00:30:37.769
you talk about politics

00:30:37.769 --> 00:30:40.605
and it's like a lot of it is
just debunking bullshit, right?

00:30:40.605 --> 00:30:43.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like the people that
just shovel all day long.

00:30:45.710 --> 00:30:46.578
- Yes, that is what
I'm trying to do.

00:30:47.912 --> 00:30:50.381
What I feel like, mate,

00:30:50.381 --> 00:30:54.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that I'm limited in my
understanding of most things.

00:30:54.719 --> 00:30:58.823
In fact, the sum total of all
human knowledge is negligible

00:30:58.823 --> 00:31:01.659 align:start size:81% position:19%
compared to the
vast limitlessness

00:31:01.659 --> 00:31:03.795
of all potential realities.

00:31:03.795 --> 00:31:07.298 align:start size:88% position:13%
So there has to be a
kind of blunt pragmatism

00:31:07.298 --> 00:31:09.834 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the way that we organize
culture and society.

00:31:09.834 --> 00:31:13.872 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the only reference
that I can access

00:31:13.872 --> 00:31:15.907
is how did we evolve?

00:31:15.907 --> 00:31:19.444
Did we evolve to live
in giant communities?

00:31:19.444 --> 00:31:20.645
I can see that there are ways

00:31:20.645 --> 00:31:22.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
where living, like
having broad alliances

00:31:22.714 --> 00:31:24.549
would be hugely beneficial.

00:31:24.549 --> 00:31:25.950
I can see that there are ways

00:31:25.950 --> 00:31:28.486 align:start position:0%
where the miracles of technology
in medicine and science

00:31:29.387 --> 00:31:31.389
are hugely, hugely applicable.

00:31:31.389 --> 00:31:33.424
Obviously, of course,
I live in the world

00:31:33.424 --> 00:31:35.927
but it seems that there
is an invisible ideology

00:31:35.927 --> 00:31:37.929
that doesn't declare and
state itself explicitly.

00:31:37.929 --> 00:31:41.532 align:start size:97% position:3%
And all of the even
apparent cultural arguments

00:31:41.532 --> 00:31:44.769
happen to take place
within its framework.

00:31:44.769 --> 00:31:46.604
And what I would call
it is commodification,

00:31:46.604 --> 00:31:49.274 align:start size:88% position:13%
consumerism, late
capitalism, corporatism,

00:31:49.274 --> 00:31:52.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
global corporatism,
neoliberalism

00:31:52.010 --> 00:31:54.212
that this ideology isn't
being openly discussed

00:31:54.212 --> 00:31:56.681 align:start size:81% position:19%
and it's at its
Nadia, it's dying.

00:31:56.681 --> 00:31:57.749
It's already dead.

00:31:57.749 --> 00:31:59.217
It died in 2008

00:31:59.217 --> 00:32:02.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now we've got something
bizarre and monstrous.

00:32:02.487 --> 00:32:04.122
- So we have like a Frankenstein

00:32:04.122 --> 00:32:05.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
trying to keep it
together or something

00:32:05.857 --> 00:32:08.660 align:start size:97% position:3%
while they were rearranging
chairs on the Titanic

00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:09.494
as it's sinking.

00:32:09.494 --> 00:32:10.428
Something like that?

00:32:10.428 --> 00:32:11.529
- Yes, that's what I feel like.

00:32:11.529 --> 00:32:12.897
Yes, that's what I feel like.

00:32:12.897 --> 00:32:14.399
And I feel like

00:32:14.399 --> 00:32:17.035
if it is not succinctly
and explicitly addressed,

00:32:17.035 --> 00:32:20.672
we are going to experience
new types of authoritarianism

00:32:20.672 --> 00:32:24.609
that frame themselves in, or
albeit apparently novel ways.

00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:28.313 align:start position:0%
That benefit hugely from
arguing about the sort of stuff,

00:32:28.313 --> 00:32:29.881
like even the stuff

00:32:29.881 --> 00:32:31.716
about like the public
schools or whatever,

00:32:31.716 --> 00:32:33.217
when plainly like that,

00:32:33.217 --> 00:32:35.720
if you said, oh, I wanna
raise my kids in this way,

00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.221
I'd go, oh, okay.

00:32:37.221 --> 00:32:39.257
And I would assume that you
would be the same with me.

00:32:39.257 --> 00:32:41.192
Like who cares?

00:32:41.192 --> 00:32:43.861 align:start size:81% position:19%
As long as it's
not sort of abuse.

00:32:43.861 --> 00:32:46.931 align:start position:0%
There seems to be some universal
ideas that we understand.

00:32:46.931 --> 00:32:48.166
- When you're traveling,

00:32:48.166 --> 00:32:50.134 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you see places that
it's working better

00:32:50.134 --> 00:32:51.669
than other places?

00:32:51.669 --> 00:32:52.637
I mean, now you've been
a couple days in Florida,

00:32:52.637 --> 00:32:53.838
but you were just in Cali

00:32:53.838 --> 00:32:55.106 align:start size:84% position:16%
where it's obviously
way different-

00:32:55.106 --> 00:32:57.642
- I did a standup
show in Clearwater.

00:32:57.642 --> 00:32:58.476
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:32:58.476 --> 00:32:59.444
- And I really liked it.

00:32:59.444 --> 00:33:01.446
And what I do recognize, yes.

00:33:01.446 --> 00:33:04.048 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I do recognize that
there's a sort of a deep sense

00:33:04.048 --> 00:33:05.984
of sort of like pride here

00:33:05.984 --> 00:33:08.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's obviously
somewhat due to the stance

00:33:08.419 --> 00:33:10.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Florida took
during the lockdown,

00:33:10.688 --> 00:33:15.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
that anti-authoritarianism
is being expressed.

00:33:16.427 --> 00:33:17.695
Like the governor

00:33:17.695 --> 00:33:21.966
is the anti-government
figure in your state.

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.168
And you know, why not?

00:33:24.168 --> 00:33:27.038 align:start position:0%
I'm not pessimistic about human
beings, generally speaking,

00:33:27.038 --> 00:33:28.373
but I would always just look

00:33:28.373 --> 00:33:29.907 align:start size:84% position:16%
at where is the
funding coming from?

00:33:29.907 --> 00:33:31.275
What's the ultimate intention?

00:33:31.275 --> 00:33:32.510
What kind of alliance?

00:33:32.510 --> 00:33:33.578
I would just ask
the same questions

00:33:33.578 --> 00:33:34.812
that I would ask of anybody.

00:33:34.812 --> 00:33:36.314
Is it as democratic as possible?

00:33:36.314 --> 00:33:41.152
And I'm like the "it's better
than" I would always reject

00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.454
from both sides, as we've said.

00:33:43.454 --> 00:33:44.789
That's what I was
sort of rejecting

00:33:44.789 --> 00:33:46.557 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the tele program
the other day.

00:33:46.557 --> 00:33:48.326
And I don't know Ron DeSantis,

00:33:48.326 --> 00:33:49.861 align:start size:81% position:19%
for all I know,
he could be Jesus.

00:33:49.861 --> 00:33:51.095
But sort of like-

00:33:51.095 --> 00:33:52.597
- I'm pretty sure
he is not Jesus,

00:33:52.597 --> 00:33:54.699 align:start size:97% position:3%
but maybe I can get you
guys to sit down for coffee.

00:33:54.699 --> 00:33:56.034 align:start size:88% position:13%
How about that?
- Yeah, God, absolutely.

00:33:56.034 --> 00:33:56.868
You know, I'd like that.

00:33:56.868 --> 00:33:57.668
I'd like that.

00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:01.472
What I do accept, Dave,

00:34:01.472 --> 00:34:05.076 align:start position:0%
is that I feel that we want
the maximum amount of authority

00:34:05.076 --> 00:34:06.577
in our own lives.

00:34:06.577 --> 00:34:08.713
Maximum personal authority
and autonomy, excuse me.

00:34:08.713 --> 00:34:11.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the maximum
amount of democracy.

00:34:11.115 --> 00:34:13.251 align:start position:0%
And like I told you at the
beginning of this conversation,

00:34:13.251 --> 00:34:15.086
I don't really like controversy.

00:34:15.086 --> 00:34:16.587
And I don't think that

00:34:16.587 --> 00:34:19.290
any of that stuff's even
particularly complicated.

00:34:19.290 --> 00:34:24.262 align:start position:0%
I'm just sort of inviting people
that identify on the right

00:34:24.262 --> 00:34:26.431
to be as discerning as
I would invite people

00:34:26.431 --> 00:34:28.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
that identify on
the left to be like.

00:34:28.433 --> 00:34:32.036
Are we definitely operating
on behalf of ordinary people?

00:34:32.036 --> 00:34:35.306 align:start size:81% position:19%
Totally inclusive,
non-judgmental,
completely loving,

00:34:35.306 --> 00:34:36.741
not secretly operating

00:34:36.741 --> 00:34:39.544 align:start size:97% position:3%
on behalf of economic
interests in some, you know-

00:34:39.544 --> 00:34:42.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Is one of those directions
easier than the other?

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:44.615 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like right now, obviously
people on the right dig you.

00:34:44.615 --> 00:34:46.517 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's I think probably
a little weird for you

00:34:46.517 --> 00:34:47.718
in some respects, right?

00:34:47.718 --> 00:34:50.488 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like people that maybe
a couple years ago

00:34:50.488 --> 00:34:52.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
you thought, ah, these weren't
my people, but they're.

00:34:52.090 --> 00:34:53.024
That's what I found.

00:34:53.024 --> 00:34:54.425
I was a lefty my whole life.

00:34:54.425 --> 00:34:55.526 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then suddenly I
started saying a few things

00:34:55.526 --> 00:34:56.694
about freedom,

00:34:56.694 --> 00:34:57.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
kind of what you're
preaching here

00:34:57.929 --> 00:34:59.730 align:start size:81% position:19%
in a probably more
simplistic way.

00:34:59.730 --> 00:35:01.232
The next thing I knew,

00:35:01.232 --> 00:35:02.467
all these people that I
thought were the bad guys

00:35:02.467 --> 00:35:04.102
were like, Hey, you
wanna have dinner?

00:35:04.102 --> 00:35:05.970
Let's see what's what.

00:35:05.970 --> 00:35:07.138
- But what I will say-

00:35:07.138 --> 00:35:08.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I like how you
switch mugs like that.

00:35:08.539 --> 00:35:09.373
(Russell laughs)

00:35:09.373 --> 00:35:10.575
What was in there?

00:35:10.575 --> 00:35:11.843
I had no idea what's in there.

00:35:11.843 --> 00:35:13.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And also it's gone
from blue to red.

00:35:13.678 --> 00:35:14.645
- Yeah.

00:35:14.645 --> 00:35:15.880
Oh, wow.

00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:17.482
- Right off our point in
the conversation, huh?

00:35:17.482 --> 00:35:20.017
Because in a way,
it doesn't matter.

00:35:20.017 --> 00:35:22.019
They're both basically the same-

00:35:22.019 --> 00:35:24.188
- How very effective, wow.

00:35:26.057 --> 00:35:29.193
- There's still statistics on
where the funding comes from,

00:35:29.193 --> 00:35:31.195
on the number of
people in Congress

00:35:31.195 --> 00:35:33.831
that own stocks and shares
in like energy companies

00:35:33.831 --> 00:35:35.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
or the military
industrial complex.

00:35:35.133 --> 00:35:37.135
It's just basically the same.

00:35:37.135 --> 00:35:38.069
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:35:38.069 --> 00:35:39.270
- It's just basically the same.

00:35:39.270 --> 00:35:40.505 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's just sort
of my position.

00:35:40.505 --> 00:35:42.073
Certainly, I've
found that people

00:35:43.541 --> 00:35:46.477
identify as being sort of
conservative or Republican

00:35:46.477 --> 00:35:49.647
or whoever have been very
open to this conversation.

00:35:49.647 --> 00:35:54.652
And look, it's clear to
me and a matter of record

00:35:56.654 --> 00:35:58.689
that about 30, 40 years ago,

00:35:58.689 --> 00:36:01.259
or maybe even earlier than that,

00:36:01.259 --> 00:36:03.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
the liberal establishment
became co-opted

00:36:03.861 --> 00:36:05.663
by the same financial interests

00:36:05.663 --> 00:36:07.732 align:start size:88% position:13%
that have traditionally
been associated

00:36:07.732 --> 00:36:09.233
with right wing politics.

00:36:09.233 --> 00:36:11.769
If you look at the conditions
that led to the war in Iraq

00:36:11.769 --> 00:36:12.870
and the kind of relationships

00:36:12.870 --> 00:36:14.872
and the kind of restructuring

00:36:14.872 --> 00:36:16.374
that took place in that country,

00:36:16.374 --> 00:36:18.309
and the catastrophe that
happened around that war,

00:36:18.309 --> 00:36:19.877
that was Janie and Bush.

00:36:19.877 --> 00:36:21.712
And now look at what's
happening elsewhere.

00:36:21.712 --> 00:36:23.247
And there are sort of,

00:36:23.247 --> 00:36:25.650 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would say, comparable
conversations that
could take place.

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:27.118
And it's pretty clear

00:36:27.118 --> 00:36:29.153 align:start size:97% position:3%
where like the sort of Clinton
Foundation gets money from

00:36:29.153 --> 00:36:31.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the way that they advocate
for particular things.

00:36:31.389 --> 00:36:36.394
So what I feel like is that
the solution will not come

00:36:37.128 --> 00:36:38.663
from within that system.

00:36:38.663 --> 00:36:41.999
I don't want to glory it by
reveling in the differences

00:36:41.999 --> 00:36:44.702
because actually
where I am from,

00:36:44.702 --> 00:36:49.106 align:start position:0%
is a normal, modest, blue
collar working class background

00:36:49.106 --> 00:36:50.708
in Essex, England.

00:36:50.708 --> 00:36:53.611
And when I see people demonized

00:36:53.611 --> 00:36:56.147
on the basis of their
class or their culture,

00:36:56.147 --> 00:36:59.250
whether they are in the
dominant cultural group

00:36:59.250 --> 00:37:01.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
sexually or racially
or culturally,

00:37:01.285 --> 00:37:06.290
or a smaller cultural
group by those markers,

00:37:07.458 --> 00:37:10.595 align:start size:84% position:16%
if economically we are
attacking people...

00:37:10.595 --> 00:37:11.762
If we're attacking a class

00:37:11.762 --> 00:37:13.698 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is economically
dispossessed,

00:37:13.698 --> 00:37:15.766
then I feel like, oh, I
see what's happening now.

00:37:15.766 --> 00:37:17.034
I see what's happening.

00:37:17.034 --> 00:37:18.703
I see why people are angry.

00:37:18.703 --> 00:37:21.005
I see why people feel that
they're being spoken down to,

00:37:21.005 --> 00:37:22.640
they are being spoken down to.

00:37:22.640 --> 00:37:24.342
And I suppose, Dave,

00:37:24.342 --> 00:37:27.345
that that's the thing that I
felt wasn't being addressed

00:37:27.345 --> 00:37:28.879
and isn't being addressed.

00:37:28.879 --> 00:37:33.384
That the blame is being put on
people that aren't empowered.

00:37:33.384 --> 00:37:36.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
And also that
there's an escalation

00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:41.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
of the kind of
accusations around, God,
what do I wanna say?

00:37:42.560 --> 00:37:44.028
Perjuring people's beliefs.

00:37:44.028 --> 00:37:45.563
Oh, those people
are just racist.

00:37:45.563 --> 00:37:47.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
Those people are
this, are just that.

00:37:47.031 --> 00:37:49.967
And I'm actually generally
quite optimistic about people

00:37:49.967 --> 00:37:51.602 align:start size:84% position:16%
and think that
people will get along

00:37:51.602 --> 00:37:53.170
if you leave them alone

00:37:53.170 --> 00:37:57.308 align:start size:97% position:3%
and if you don't impecuniate
them and impoverish them.

00:37:57.308 --> 00:37:59.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you think a
whole bunch of people

00:37:59.043 --> 00:38:00.711
are just gonna kind of
check out of the system?

00:38:00.711 --> 00:38:01.946
Because I think a lot of people

00:38:01.946 --> 00:38:03.447 align:start size:81% position:19%
intuitively get
what you're saying

00:38:03.447 --> 00:38:05.216
and they really do want to
live and let live thing.

00:38:05.216 --> 00:38:06.717
I think there really
is a feeling of that

00:38:06.717 --> 00:38:08.219
in America right now.

00:38:08.219 --> 00:38:10.321
That the whole system is so
screwed up, it's so wacky,

00:38:10.321 --> 00:38:14.258 align:start position:0%
it's not in it for anyone
except the few that control it.

00:38:14.258 --> 00:38:15.793
I think a lot of people
are just gonna be like,

00:38:15.793 --> 00:38:17.128 align:start size:81% position:19%
all right, I'm
just checking out,

00:38:17.128 --> 00:38:18.863
I'm deleting the accounts,

00:38:18.863 --> 00:38:20.765
I'm figuring out how
to get off the grid

00:38:20.765 --> 00:38:22.767
and just really just
kind of disappearing.

00:38:22.767 --> 00:38:25.636
I think it's probably
happening as we speak.

00:38:25.636 --> 00:38:26.971
- I wonder about that movement.

00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:28.306
I wonder about sort of

00:38:28.306 --> 00:38:32.209 align:start size:97% position:3%
a second kind of
declaration of independence.

00:38:32.209 --> 00:38:33.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like what would happen
if people did that?

00:38:33.944 --> 00:38:35.446
Our community,

00:38:35.446 --> 00:38:38.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
we are no longer associating
with the super structure.

00:38:38.382 --> 00:38:41.485
We want our own new confederacy.

00:38:41.485 --> 00:38:43.521
- Have you heard
of that in America?

00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:44.455
They're talking about it now.

00:38:44.455 --> 00:38:45.723
Texas, there's some congressmen

00:38:45.723 --> 00:38:48.893
that put forward a bill
to have a succession

00:38:48.893 --> 00:38:50.494
and just get out of the union

00:38:50.494 --> 00:38:53.597
and that maybe some of the
red states could move out,

00:38:53.597 --> 00:38:54.632
something like that.

00:38:54.632 --> 00:38:57.234
It seems like we're united,

00:38:57.234 --> 00:38:58.169
but what are we united by?

00:38:58.169 --> 00:38:59.670
It's hard to figure out-

00:38:59.670 --> 00:39:01.372
- I wonder.

00:39:01.372 --> 00:39:02.506
Yeah, I guess that's
a conversation that
needs to carry on.

00:39:02.506 --> 00:39:04.775 align:start size:88% position:13%
It needn't be presented
as adversarial-

00:39:04.775 --> 00:39:06.143
- Right, that's the thing.

00:39:06.143 --> 00:39:07.745 align:start size:97% position:3%
It comes off as adversarial,
but it shouldn't.

00:39:09.180 --> 00:39:13.751
- In our country, which is
obviously an absurd term

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:15.353
because a country is a concept.

00:39:15.353 --> 00:39:16.587
What is it really?

00:39:16.587 --> 00:39:18.456 align:start size:88% position:13%
A flag, a set of beliefs
of a group of people?

00:39:18.456 --> 00:39:20.858 align:start size:97% position:3%
If it isn't benefiting those
people, what is it doing?

00:39:20.858 --> 00:39:22.193
- That land mass
across the pond-

00:39:22.193 --> 00:39:23.361
- You see that thing?

00:39:23.361 --> 00:39:25.262 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you know this
language you're using?

00:39:25.262 --> 00:39:29.200 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like the devolution
was a big conversation

00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:32.236
like a few years ago.

00:39:32.236 --> 00:39:33.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Scottish
independence is discussed

00:39:33.971 --> 00:39:35.406
and Wales has an assembly.

00:39:35.406 --> 00:39:39.443 align:start position:0%
And obviously, because of
colonization and imperialism era

00:39:39.443 --> 00:39:41.245
in the north of that country,

00:39:41.245 --> 00:39:45.683 align:start size:97% position:3%
and because Britain is an
imperial and colonial power,

00:39:45.683 --> 00:39:49.019 align:start position:0%
historically, these
conversations have been ongoing.

00:39:49.019 --> 00:39:51.789
And I feel like if
these institutions

00:39:51.789 --> 00:39:53.858
do not exist for the
benefit of the people

00:39:53.858 --> 00:39:55.092
that they claim to serve,

00:39:55.092 --> 00:39:56.861
what is it that they are doing?

00:39:56.861 --> 00:40:00.097
And I think that's
the type of inquiry

00:40:00.097 --> 00:40:02.533
that I don't claim
to have the answer to

00:40:02.533 --> 00:40:04.034
or the conclusions to,

00:40:04.034 --> 00:40:06.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I feel that that
ought be the investigation

00:40:06.337 --> 00:40:07.605
that takes place.

00:40:07.605 --> 00:40:09.106
And it oughtn't be disingenuous

00:40:09.106 --> 00:40:12.309
and it oughtn't be a sort of
sly way of masking corporatism

00:40:12.309 --> 00:40:15.212 align:start size:88% position:13%
or allowing people to
avoid this or evade that

00:40:15.212 --> 00:40:16.747
or benefit from this.

00:40:16.747 --> 00:40:21.318
The term that keeps occurring
to me as such is "good faith."

00:40:21.318 --> 00:40:22.853 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's have good
faith conversations.

00:40:22.853 --> 00:40:24.588 align:start size:88% position:13%
Oh look, we're different
from one another.

00:40:24.588 --> 00:40:26.123
How do you wanna organize this?

00:40:26.123 --> 00:40:30.161
How do you think the people
best can behave collegiately?

00:40:30.161 --> 00:40:31.829
What's the sort of critical mass

00:40:31.829 --> 00:40:33.497
before this gets a
little complicated?

00:40:33.497 --> 00:40:36.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because the tendency appears
to be economically led,

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:39.270
globalism currently
becoming instituted

00:40:39.270 --> 00:40:42.406
in an attempt to create
a unipolar hedge money

00:40:42.406 --> 00:40:43.541
through various means

00:40:43.541 --> 00:40:44.842
and an inability to accept

00:40:44.842 --> 00:40:47.077
that there are a
variety of cultures

00:40:47.077 --> 00:40:48.913
that sort of are
independently vying

00:40:48.913 --> 00:40:50.414
for their right to exist.

00:40:50.414 --> 00:40:52.716 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You ever worry we're in
that dystopian future already?

00:40:52.716 --> 00:40:54.385
Like we're too deep in it

00:40:54.385 --> 00:40:56.787 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the point where we don't
even know we're in it exactly.

00:40:56.787 --> 00:40:58.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Skynet's
basically been turned on,

00:40:58.823 --> 00:41:00.524
the machine is operating

00:41:00.524 --> 00:41:01.792
and we're kind of
all in the matrix.

00:41:01.792 --> 00:41:03.294
We have these little glimmers.

00:41:03.294 --> 00:41:05.863
I kind of think it's why your
clip on Real Time took off.

00:41:05.863 --> 00:41:08.165 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was like a little
glimmer of truth

00:41:08.165 --> 00:41:09.867
amongst all of the lies.

00:41:09.867 --> 00:41:13.003 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we see it and then we
all get lost in the BS again.

00:41:13.003 --> 00:41:14.939 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then you wait
for another glimmer,

00:41:14.939 --> 00:41:17.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you sort of just never
get out of the slumber.

00:41:17.708 --> 00:41:18.542
Something like that.

00:41:18.542 --> 00:41:20.077
- Yeah, I do feel that.

00:41:20.077 --> 00:41:23.047
But I also deeply believe in
the possibility of awakening

00:41:23.047 --> 00:41:24.482 align:start size:81% position:19%
and what I haven't
mentioned yet,

00:41:24.482 --> 00:41:27.117
because I guess, I
tend to communicate

00:41:27.117 --> 00:41:29.820 align:start size:97% position:3%
in accordance with the
context that I find myself in,

00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:33.023
is that most of
what I believe in

00:41:33.023 --> 00:41:36.193
is undergirded by
spiritual beliefs

00:41:36.193 --> 00:41:37.695
rather than political ones.

00:41:37.695 --> 00:41:38.529
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:41:38.529 --> 00:41:39.463
- I don't actually...

00:41:39.463 --> 00:41:41.131
You know, all I know politically

00:41:41.131 --> 00:41:42.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
is just sort of just
a conversational
layman's knowledge.

00:41:42.933 --> 00:41:44.335
Like you know what I mean?

00:41:44.335 --> 00:41:46.704 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've not been through
higher education,

00:41:46.704 --> 00:41:48.372
I've not been to university,

00:41:48.372 --> 00:41:49.874
I don't claim to know

00:41:49.874 --> 00:41:53.777 align:start size:97% position:3%
any more than anybody that's
just watching this now.

00:41:53.777 --> 00:41:55.980
- But that's why your
politics is interesting

00:41:55.980 --> 00:41:57.781
because it doesn't
come from politics,

00:41:57.781 --> 00:41:59.183
it's obviously coming
from something else.

00:41:59.183 --> 00:42:00.885
That's why I think it's hitting.

00:42:00.885 --> 00:42:03.587
- It comes from a sense of
like that as human beings,

00:42:03.587 --> 00:42:05.956
we know that we need
meaning and purpose.

00:42:05.956 --> 00:42:09.960 align:start size:97% position:3%
We know that we have this
sort of yearning for freedom,

00:42:09.960 --> 00:42:13.063 align:start size:97% position:3%
freedom of expression, freedom
to be who we really are.

00:42:13.063 --> 00:42:16.700
We also know that there are
a myriad ways of being human.

00:42:16.700 --> 00:42:21.205
And that there seems to be
some scarce remembered time

00:42:21.205 --> 00:42:23.440
where we could live differently.

00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:26.176
There seems to be an awareness
that we are not at the apex,

00:42:26.176 --> 00:42:28.078
but we are at the
end of something.

00:42:28.078 --> 00:42:30.247
That this could go either way.

00:42:30.247 --> 00:42:33.951
That we could yield to more
centralizing authoritarianism

00:42:33.951 --> 00:42:35.653
or we could look at
different models.

00:42:35.653 --> 00:42:38.889 align:start size:88% position:13%
That there may be
information in the past,

00:42:38.889 --> 00:42:42.860
deep, deep in the past, arcane,
anthropological information.

00:42:42.860 --> 00:42:46.130
There may be even in the
genius of Thomas Paine

00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:48.198 align:start size:84% position:16%
and your founding
fathers and all that,

00:42:48.198 --> 00:42:51.235
stuff that's of real value.

00:42:51.235 --> 00:42:52.503
But certainly,

00:42:52.503 --> 00:42:55.205
there needs to be some
new principles enacted.

00:42:55.205 --> 00:42:59.410
And I think that even to move
forward into that territory,

00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:02.613
we might have to
offer one another

00:43:02.613 --> 00:43:07.151
the grace of a certain
amount of discordance.

00:43:07.151 --> 00:43:08.719
- So what do you do if a
certain amount of people

00:43:08.719 --> 00:43:10.220
don't want to offer that grace?

00:43:10.220 --> 00:43:11.755
Because again, I'm with you

00:43:11.755 --> 00:43:13.357
and I think a lot of people
watching this are with you-

00:43:13.357 --> 00:43:14.425
- Violent war, Dave.

00:43:14.425 --> 00:43:15.593
(both laugh)

00:43:15.593 --> 00:43:17.161 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You have to take
camps, I assume, right?

00:43:17.161 --> 00:43:20.064
No, but what do you do if
you sit down with the...

00:43:20.064 --> 00:43:21.265
You know, if Florida was like,

00:43:21.265 --> 00:43:22.933
"Hey, we've just
kind of had enough.

00:43:22.933 --> 00:43:24.868 align:start size:84% position:16%
No offense, we're just
gonna do our thing

00:43:24.868 --> 00:43:26.170
and take care of our people.

00:43:26.170 --> 00:43:27.404 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's gonna be very
pleasant here.

00:43:27.404 --> 00:43:30.274
Let everybody live as
free as they want."

00:43:30.274 --> 00:43:31.809 align:start size:84% position:16%
But if the other guys
just keep saying,

00:43:31.809 --> 00:43:34.645
"no, no, no, no, no, no, no,
we still want some of that.

00:43:34.645 --> 00:43:35.879
We want some of the cash,

00:43:35.879 --> 00:43:37.581
we want some of the
goodness, we want..."

00:43:37.581 --> 00:43:39.016
What do you do then?

00:43:39.016 --> 00:43:41.051 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I suppose then
Florida would have to-

00:43:41.051 --> 00:43:42.486
- Because I think a lot of
people are thinking about it.

00:43:42.486 --> 00:43:44.154 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think the ordinary
people of each of the states

00:43:44.154 --> 00:43:45.222
would have to...

00:43:45.222 --> 00:43:46.724
It has been long argued,

00:43:46.724 --> 00:43:49.293
typically, I would have
to say from the left,

00:43:49.293 --> 00:43:51.328
that the ordinary
people of the world

00:43:51.328 --> 00:43:53.397
have more in common
with one another

00:43:53.397 --> 00:43:56.567 align:start size:88% position:13%
than they have with
the elites that govern.

00:43:56.567 --> 00:44:00.337 align:start position:0%
And that this has the potential
of being communicated now

00:44:00.337 --> 00:44:03.807
through the miracles that
we are currently enjoying.

00:44:05.009 --> 00:44:07.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
In his book, The
Revolt of the Public,

00:44:07.611 --> 00:44:09.713
Martin Gurri, the
former CIA analyst

00:44:09.713 --> 00:44:11.982
who you should have on your
show if you haven't already.

00:44:11.982 --> 00:44:13.250
- No, no I haven't.

00:44:13.250 --> 00:44:14.885
- Yeah, he's good man.

00:44:14.885 --> 00:44:19.223 align:start size:84% position:16%
He says that just
the technology, the
medium in a Malcolm...

00:44:19.223 --> 00:44:20.924
What am I trying to say?

00:44:20.924 --> 00:44:22.593
Malcolm McLeod-

00:44:22.593 --> 00:44:24.128 align:start size:97% position:3%
- The medium is the message.
- The message.

00:44:24.128 --> 00:44:25.696
Yeah, yeah.

00:44:25.696 --> 00:44:28.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like that what we
are experiencing now

00:44:28.899 --> 00:44:30.701
is the ability to communicate,

00:44:30.701 --> 00:44:35.105 align:start position:0%
to discern in new ways that
power is organizing differently.

00:44:35.105 --> 00:44:37.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
That you can't centralize
and control in the same way.

00:44:37.141 --> 00:44:40.210 align:start size:97% position:3%
So new forms of
authoritarianism are emerging.

00:44:41.045 --> 00:44:42.780
And we've already seen

00:44:42.780 --> 00:44:44.882
through Napster and the
Arab Spring and Occupy,

00:44:44.882 --> 00:44:46.283
the potential for organization

00:44:46.283 --> 00:44:48.452
almost spontaneously.

00:44:48.452 --> 00:44:50.988 align:start size:97% position:3%
That I would say that
these are the conversations

00:44:50.988 --> 00:44:52.256
I'm having now.

00:44:52.256 --> 00:44:53.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the reason that
I'm having them

00:44:53.857 --> 00:44:55.159
is that if like why even...

00:44:55.159 --> 00:44:57.628 align:start size:84% position:16%
You could even reject
