00:52:56.973 --> 00:52:58.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It would be the exact
amount, you're right there.

00:52:58.909 --> 00:53:01.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
You're right at the precipice
of being the bad guy.

00:53:01.845 --> 00:53:03.980
- After that there's gotta
be some real redistribution.

00:53:03.980 --> 00:53:05.182
- Yeah.

00:53:05.182 --> 00:53:06.550
- Yeah.

00:53:06.550 --> 00:53:09.186 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you find that
all the basic problems

00:53:09.186 --> 00:53:10.554
of everything we're
talking about here,

00:53:10.554 --> 00:53:12.389 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether you're back
home in the UK or here,

00:53:12.389 --> 00:53:13.890
that it basically is the same?

00:53:13.890 --> 00:53:16.293 align:start size:88% position:13%
That the way we all
talk about the problems

00:53:16.293 --> 00:53:18.061
now has become global?

00:53:20.997 --> 00:53:23.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It feels like
there's some variety.

00:53:23.133 --> 00:53:24.367
What I wonder is,

00:53:25.235 --> 00:53:27.270
I ask myself, would I be happier

00:53:27.270 --> 00:53:30.006 align:start size:84% position:16%
if I lived a life
of complete service?

00:53:30.006 --> 00:53:31.374
Would I be happier?

00:53:31.374 --> 00:53:32.842
Is it working for me?

00:53:32.842 --> 00:53:34.778
Are the systems working,

00:53:34.778 --> 00:53:37.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
the systems of
personal gratification?

00:53:37.714 --> 00:53:38.982
I've improved a lot.

00:53:38.982 --> 00:53:41.851
I don't live how I used to live.

00:53:41.851 --> 00:53:44.454 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's the question
that I ask of myself is,

00:53:44.454 --> 00:53:46.856 align:start size:88% position:13%
do things seem different
in different places?

00:53:46.856 --> 00:53:48.091
I suppose so,

00:53:48.091 --> 00:53:51.928 align:start size:88% position:13%
but there does also seem
to be a general sense

00:53:51.928 --> 00:53:53.797
that is quite global.

00:53:53.797 --> 00:53:57.434 align:start position:0%
And I don't know what it's
like in Pakistan or Luxembourg,

00:53:57.434 --> 00:54:00.070
but like in the places
that I go to and know,

00:54:00.070 --> 00:54:03.306 align:start size:97% position:3%
I feel like there is a hunger
and appetite and unease,

00:54:03.306 --> 00:54:06.710
a sense of atrophy.

00:54:06.710 --> 00:54:11.681
And most cultures talk
about ages and epochs

00:54:11.681 --> 00:54:15.585
and identifiable
periods and trends.

00:54:15.585 --> 00:54:17.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
And of course, perhaps there's
even an narcissism to that

00:54:17.954 --> 00:54:20.924
because all of us are going
to experience Armageddon,

00:54:20.924 --> 00:54:22.592
we are all going to die.

00:54:22.592 --> 00:54:24.494
And I do query sometimes, Dave,

00:54:24.494 --> 00:54:25.362
whether it matters-

00:54:25.362 --> 00:54:26.830
- Even in Florida?

00:54:26.830 --> 00:54:28.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we'll be okay
here from the death thing-

00:54:28.598 --> 00:54:29.966
- Especially in Florida,

00:54:29.966 --> 00:54:31.668
looking at some of
the demographic.

00:54:31.668 --> 00:54:36.673 align:start position:0%
Like I feel that perhaps
there's a kind of vanity to it,

00:54:38.141 --> 00:54:40.243
does it matter if everyone
dies simultaneously or not

00:54:40.243 --> 00:54:42.178
if the planet is going
to ultimately expire?

00:54:42.178 --> 00:54:43.980
But I do believe in the
sanctity of human life,

00:54:43.980 --> 00:54:47.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do believe in the
unique beauty of our kind,

00:54:47.917 --> 00:54:49.986
of our species and
I do believe in God.

00:54:49.986 --> 00:54:51.221
And I do believe that we're here

00:54:51.221 --> 00:54:54.124
to realize something
valuable and beautiful

00:54:54.124 --> 00:54:55.892 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that we should
be aspirational

00:54:55.892 --> 00:54:57.360 align:start size:84% position:16%
in our relationships
with one another.

00:54:57.360 --> 00:55:01.298
And for me, as we were
discussing earlier today,

00:55:01.298 --> 00:55:03.667
if it isn't based in action,

00:55:03.667 --> 00:55:07.170 align:start position:0%
like if your experience of
love and devotion in the divine

00:55:07.170 --> 00:55:09.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
doesn't have some
expression in your behavior,

00:55:09.773 --> 00:55:11.775
then it's fantasy.

00:55:11.775 --> 00:55:13.009
- Do you have parts of your life

00:55:13.009 --> 00:55:14.778
that you haven't kind
of put together yet?

00:55:14.778 --> 00:55:16.446
- Yeah, the whole thing really.

00:55:16.446 --> 00:55:18.114
I'm still trying to
just work it all out.

00:55:18.114 --> 00:55:19.716
I'm still trying
to work it all out.

00:55:19.716 --> 00:55:22.619
I've recognized that
when I'm sort of...

00:55:22.619 --> 00:55:24.287
I'm quite tired today,

00:55:24.287 --> 00:55:28.158
I'm a bit worn out and it's
almost a little bit tearful,

00:55:28.158 --> 00:55:31.728
but like I recognize that I
have a facility for language

00:55:31.728 --> 00:55:33.229
that could perhaps mask the fact

00:55:33.229 --> 00:55:36.733 align:start position:0%
that I acknowledge that I don't
really know what I'm doing.

00:55:36.733 --> 00:55:38.468
I'm just asking some questions.

00:55:38.468 --> 00:55:39.936
I don't actually think

00:55:39.936 --> 00:55:41.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
that anyone else knows
what they're doing either.

00:55:41.071 --> 00:55:42.539
That's what I've always thought

00:55:42.539 --> 00:55:44.441
when like I'm dealing with
sort of political demagogues,

00:55:44.441 --> 00:55:46.576
like sort of Boris
Johnson or anybody,

00:55:46.576 --> 00:55:47.744
no one knows.

00:55:47.744 --> 00:55:48.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Dave] Yeah.
- What do you know?

00:55:48.545 --> 00:55:49.446
What does anybody know?

00:55:50.847 --> 00:55:52.315 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know like there are people
that are expert plumbers

00:55:52.315 --> 00:55:55.018
and expert in construction
and medicine and all of that,

00:55:55.018 --> 00:55:56.853 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that there are different
fields of expertise.

00:55:56.853 --> 00:56:00.290
But all of this for me leads
to the smallest possible model.

00:56:00.290 --> 00:56:02.258
Smallest possible
business model.

00:56:03.460 --> 00:56:04.928
Smallest possible
democratic models,

00:56:04.928 --> 00:56:07.764
most ability to organize
your own life possible.

00:56:07.764 --> 00:56:09.332
Not like that life
becomes abstract

00:56:09.332 --> 00:56:11.735 align:start size:88% position:13%
and your role is to sort
of stare at a screen

00:56:11.735 --> 00:56:13.636
and participate only
through consuming.

00:56:13.636 --> 00:56:15.572
So you don't have any role

00:56:15.572 --> 00:56:19.075 align:start position:0%
other than the abstract
expressions of your own outrage.

00:56:19.075 --> 00:56:20.310
- Yeah.

00:56:20.310 --> 00:56:21.878
The famous quote,
by Solzhenitsyn,

00:56:21.878 --> 00:56:23.380
"and all that we have to..."

00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:24.948
In essence, I'm gonna
slightly butcher it,

00:56:24.948 --> 00:56:26.149
but we just have-

00:56:26.149 --> 00:56:28.151 align:start size:84% position:16%
- He went through
worse in them Gulags.

00:56:28.151 --> 00:56:29.386
- Those Gulags were rough.

00:56:29.386 --> 00:56:30.587
But basically he said,

00:56:30.587 --> 00:56:31.988
all we have to do to end this

00:56:31.988 --> 00:56:34.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
is stop participating
in the lie.

00:56:34.190 --> 00:56:36.426
And it seems like
everyone basically

00:56:36.426 --> 00:56:39.396
is participating in the
lie, even accidentally.

00:56:39.396 --> 00:56:43.066
And I mean that for us, guys
that are responding to stuff

00:56:43.066 --> 00:56:45.902 align:start position:0%
because it's out there and
we're trying to make sense of it

00:56:45.902 --> 00:56:47.737
for people or for ourselves,

00:56:47.737 --> 00:56:50.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
and yet we still have
to participate in a game

00:56:50.807 --> 00:56:52.041
that's pretty dirty.

00:56:52.041 --> 00:56:53.843
- Well, that's what
I have been saying

00:56:53.843 --> 00:56:56.146
in these conversations,

00:56:56.146 --> 00:56:59.849
explicitly, in the
case with Joe Rogan.

00:56:59.849 --> 00:57:01.785
And now I will say to you,

00:57:01.785 --> 00:57:03.286
perhaps it isn't enough

00:57:03.286 --> 00:57:06.923
for us to engage only in
punditry or even advocacy.

00:57:06.923 --> 00:57:09.058
Perhaps it has to become,

00:57:09.058 --> 00:57:11.895 align:start size:81% position:19%
alright then let's
try and build.

00:57:11.895 --> 00:57:13.963 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, I think that there
should be communities

00:57:13.963 --> 00:57:15.832
of like subgroups of around,

00:57:15.832 --> 00:57:17.066
I don't know, is it
a hundred people?

00:57:17.066 --> 00:57:19.202
That's what chimpanzees
seem to do well with.

00:57:19.202 --> 00:57:22.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
What that 2% of DNAs
gotta afford us something.

00:57:22.172 --> 00:57:25.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe we can run slightly
larger communities.

00:57:25.008 --> 00:57:26.776
What are the general principles?

00:57:26.776 --> 00:57:28.945 align:start size:88% position:13%
What is the amount of
power you want to yield?

00:57:28.945 --> 00:57:31.414 align:start size:88% position:13%
How many ways are there
of organizing this?

00:57:31.414 --> 00:57:34.284
How much can we leave
one another alone?

00:57:34.284 --> 00:57:38.555 align:start size:97% position:3%
Perhaps we do need to be
involved in a new confederacy-

00:57:38.555 --> 00:57:40.423
- That's why I built this thing.

00:57:40.423 --> 00:57:41.724
That's why I built this thing.

00:57:41.724 --> 00:57:42.926
I mean I built this company,

00:57:42.926 --> 00:57:45.261
we merged with Rumble
to do exactly this

00:57:45.261 --> 00:57:46.095
at the digital level.

00:57:46.095 --> 00:57:47.397
I haven't built my own-

00:57:47.397 --> 00:57:48.898
- It'd be good if you
just meant this sign-

00:57:48.898 --> 00:57:50.066
- I meant this sign.

00:57:50.066 --> 00:57:51.301 align:start size:84% position:16%
I put this together,
I built this.

00:57:51.301 --> 00:57:52.302
It's pretty nice, right?

00:57:52.302 --> 00:57:53.236
It's sturdy.

00:57:53.236 --> 00:57:54.904
Come on, that's a sturdy sign.

00:57:54.904 --> 00:57:56.372 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Very satisfying,
it's brilliant.

00:57:56.372 --> 00:57:57.841
I really like it, well done.

00:57:57.841 --> 00:57:59.075
I mean, but also it's a-

00:57:59.075 --> 00:58:00.310
- But that is what
you mean, right?

00:58:00.310 --> 00:58:01.544 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like that we have
to build new things.

00:58:01.544 --> 00:58:02.979
You don't just mean
physical communities,

00:58:02.979 --> 00:58:05.014 align:start position:0%
you mean like we have to rebuild
sort of everything, right?

00:58:05.014 --> 00:58:06.115
- Yes.

00:58:06.115 --> 00:58:07.283
- That's a lot of work.

00:58:07.283 --> 00:58:08.818
- I know,

00:58:08.818 --> 00:58:10.520
but like maybe if we were all
doing just our own little bit

00:58:10.520 --> 00:58:12.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
then it's sort of
manageable, isn't it?

00:58:12.088 --> 00:58:14.023
I mean, again, that's another
thing I get from recovery.

00:58:14.023 --> 00:58:17.594 align:start size:97% position:3%
The idea that we're all a
bit mental and a bit broken,

00:58:17.594 --> 00:58:19.229
but not at the same time.

00:58:19.229 --> 00:58:20.997
And it's nice to be able
to reach out to someone

00:58:20.997 --> 00:58:22.499
and say I'm having a bit of a...

00:58:22.499 --> 00:58:25.101
Like we can connect not at
the point of our posturing,

00:58:25.101 --> 00:58:26.970
but at the point of
our vulnerability.

00:58:26.970 --> 00:58:28.938
So actually like, I don't know.

00:58:28.938 --> 00:58:29.906
I don't know what to do.

00:58:29.906 --> 00:58:30.773
What do you think?

00:58:30.773 --> 00:58:31.674
It seems you're...

00:58:32.942 --> 00:58:34.844
I had any experience once

00:58:34.844 --> 00:58:39.015 align:start position:0%
where I stopped to help a
person who had had an accident.

00:58:39.015 --> 00:58:40.517
It wasn't a serious accident.

00:58:40.517 --> 00:58:42.819
She'd only banged her head
a bit in a car in the UK

00:58:42.819 --> 00:58:44.687
and I was sort of helping,

00:58:44.687 --> 00:58:48.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
like 'cause I stopped
because it's a human duty

00:58:48.291 --> 00:58:50.426
and lots of other
people stopped too.

00:58:50.426 --> 00:58:52.529
And like it was an
interesting community

00:58:52.529 --> 00:58:54.731 align:start size:81% position:19%
that formed around
that accident.

00:58:54.731 --> 00:58:58.535 align:start position:0%
And an off duty paramedic
ultimately arrived at the scene.

00:58:58.535 --> 00:59:00.169
And I saw that in that instance,

00:59:00.169 --> 00:59:02.939
that is the person that
you want in authority.

00:59:02.939 --> 00:59:03.740
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:59:03.740 --> 00:59:04.674
- But moments later,

00:59:04.674 --> 00:59:05.875
someone else might be required

00:59:05.875 --> 00:59:07.677 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be in a position
of authority.

00:59:07.677 --> 00:59:10.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
So having intransigent
systems of power

00:59:10.179 --> 00:59:12.649
that are based on the assumption

00:59:12.649 --> 00:59:16.286
that human beings need to
be marshaled compliantly

00:59:16.286 --> 00:59:19.589
into community or
into behaving well,

00:59:19.589 --> 00:59:20.957
I am at odds with.

00:59:20.957 --> 00:59:22.759
And you say libertarianism

00:59:22.759 --> 00:59:25.161 align:start size:97% position:3%
and as I understand that
that means individual freedom

00:59:25.161 --> 00:59:26.663 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the most freedom
as an individual.

00:59:26.663 --> 00:59:27.931
Whether that's the freedom

00:59:27.931 --> 00:59:29.866
to express your sexual
identity consensually,

00:59:29.866 --> 00:59:31.134
or the freedom to express

00:59:31.134 --> 00:59:33.036
whatever aspect of
yourself that is.

00:59:33.036 --> 00:59:35.371 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what I understand
of anarchism,

00:59:35.371 --> 00:59:38.508 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's about the maximum
amount of democracy

00:59:38.508 --> 00:59:42.211
and the least amount of
dominion by organization

00:59:42.211 --> 00:59:44.113
happening at the
level of community.

00:59:44.113 --> 00:59:45.515
And the people that I admire,

00:59:45.515 --> 00:59:47.383
women like Helena Norberg-Hodge

00:59:47.383 --> 00:59:49.152 align:start size:81% position:19%
for years has been
advocating for,

00:59:49.152 --> 00:59:51.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
